<LanguageData>
  
  <!-- EN: chemfuel silo -->
  <DMSE_FuelSiloTank.label>液态燃料筒仓</DMSE_FuelSiloTank.label>
  <!-- EN: A large storage tank for storing liquid fuels uses multiple layers of metal plates and special alloys to store pressurized liquefied fuel within the tank. It provides robust protection while also holding a large amount of fuel, and supplies it to the thrusters of a gravship or the transfer engines of a ship built from structural piles. -->
  <DMSE_FuelSiloTank.description>一种用於储存液态燃料的大型储槽，采用多层金属板与特殊合金结构，可在槽体内安全存放加压液化燃料。它在提供良好防护的同时，也为重力船上的推进器或结构桩船舰上的转移引擎供应大量燃料。</DMSE_FuelSiloTank.description>
  <!-- EN: Chemfuel -->
  <DMSE_FuelSiloTank.comps.CompRefuelable.fuelGizmoLabel>化合燃料</DMSE_FuelSiloTank.comps.CompRefuelable.fuelGizmoLabel>
  <!-- EN: Chemfuel -->
  <DMSE_FuelSiloTank.comps.CompRefuelable.fuelLabel>液态燃料</DMSE_FuelSiloTank.comps.CompRefuelable.fuelLabel>
  
  <!-- EN: Fusion reactor -->
  <DMSE_FusionCore.label>聚变反应炉</DMSE_FusionCore.label>
  <!-- EN: A highly mature compact tokamak fusion reactor, commonly found in colonial fleets and ships used in the Enlightened World, has a built-in supercritical carbon dioxide turbine to provide power for its own cycle and ship equipment. However, its most crucial function is to preheat the ship's nuclear thermal propulsion system so that it can reach its maximum design power to move small-mass celestial bodies.\n\nOn a ship built from structural piles, each working fusion reactor supports up to two nuclear thermal thrusters. -->
  <DMSE_FusionCore.description>一种高度成熟的紧凑型托卡马克聚变反应炉，常见於殖民舰队与启迪世界所使用的各式舰船。其内建超临界二氧化碳涡轮发电机组，可为自身循环系统与船舰设备提供电力。不过它最关键的用途是为船舰的核热推进系统进行预热，使其能达到最大设计功率来推动大质量天体移动到新的位置。\n\n在以结构桩建造的船上，每座运作中的聚变反应炉最多可支援两具核热推进器。</DMSE_FusionCore.description>
  
  <!-- EN: Nuclear thermal thruster -->
  <DMSE_NuclearThruster.label>核热推进器</DMSE_NuclearThruster.label>
  <!-- EN: A heavy nuclear-thermal rocket thruster that generates thrust by heating liquid hydrogen through nuclear Fusion. Its specific impulse is more than twice that of conventional chemical rockets. These high-thrust engines are commonly used on interstellar tugs to perform major orbital transfers for massive platforms. Because launch operation produces substantial radioactive contamination, this engine is designed for non-atmospheric use only.\n\nBefore the Tanaka-Johnson drive was introduced, humanity used this class of thruster to accelerate the first sublight ship to the Alpha Centauri system to 20% of light speed, and received the first selfie from outside the Solar System ten years later.\n\nTransfer engine: very high thrust and low fuel use, but it needs support from a working fusion reactor on the same ship (one reactor supports two thrusters). -->
  <DMSE_NuclearThruster.description>一种重型核热火箭推进器，透过核分裂加热液态氢来产生推力，其比冲是传统化学火箭推进器的两倍以上。这类大推力推进器经常用於星际拖船，使其能为质量庞大的轨道平台进行较大幅度的轨道转移。由於起飞时会制造大量放射性污染，这类引擎被设计为无法在大气环境内使用。\n\n在田中-约翰逊引擎问世以前，人类便是透过这种推进器将第一艘前往半人马座星系的亚光速飞船加速到光速的20%，并在10年後传回人类於太阳系外的第一张自拍照。\n\n转移引擎：推力极大且燃耗低，但需要同一艘船上运作中的聚变反应炉支援（每座反应炉可支援两具）。</DMSE_NuclearThruster.description>
  
  <!-- EN: rocket booster -->
  <DMSE_SolidRocketThruster.label>火箭助推器</DMSE_SolidRocketThruster.label>
  <!-- EN: A simple and reliable disposable thruster. It provides thrust by premixing fuel and oxidizer into a solid propellant grain, which burns upon ignition to generate high-temperature gas. It has a rapid start-up capability. It is commonly used as a rocket booster or initial propulsion for strategic missiles on many pre-spacer planets, and is also frequently used as a temporary range extension for small and medium-sized ships during suborbital flight. -->
  <DMSE_SolidRocketThruster.description>一种结构简单且可靠的一次性固态燃料推进器。它将燃料与氧化剂预先混合为固体推进药柱，点火後燃烧产生高温燃气以提供推力，具备快速启动的特性。在许多前太空时代星球上，它常被用作火箭助推器或战略飞弹的初始动力，也常作为中小型舰船进行亚轨道飞行时的临时增程手段。\n\n在以结构桩建造的船上，它会在转移飞行的离轨点火时提供额外推力，提高起飞推重比且不消耗船上燃料，离轨点火结束后烧毁。可建造在平台上。</DMSE_SolidRocketThruster.description>
  
</LanguageData>